---
const cards = [
  {
    title: 'Peer-to-peer data plane',
    body:
      'The coordinator never carries traffic. An agent opens an authenticated tunnel straight to a node; the node enforces the SSRF guard and the Tor-style exit policy (port 25 and other abuse ports blocked) before any byte is relayed.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Capped spend hold, non-custodial',
    body:
      'open_session_with_hold locks a time-boxed escrow from the client allowance. The node holds a guaranteed claim up to the cap, the client can never be charged more, and any remainder is refunded automatically.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Two signatures per settlement',
    body:
      'The client proposes the byte counters and the node confirms the same values. A mismatch fails on chain, so traffic can be neither invented nor underpaid.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Pricing anyone can verify',
    body:
      'Residential and datacenter rates and the immutable 20% protocol fee live in contract storage, with change events. The values the UI shows are the values enforced on chain.',
  },
];
---

<section id="model" class="alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Built for agents, not another VPN</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">
      The coordinator is limited to signaling, the node directory and liveness heartbeats.
      Requests, data and payments move peer to peer under contract-enforced rules.
    </p>
    <div class="grid g3">
      {cards.map((c) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
          <p>{c.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
